# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Sanggyu Chong et al. (2026). Resolving the body-order paradox of machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0303302  arXiv:2509.14146v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2509.14146v2 (sha256 4d3738fe97fface2...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 643 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/chong2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: SOAP-BPNN, MACE and PET models trained on FHI-aims PBE
# hydrogen 8-mers sampled from low- and high-density bulk hydrogen, on
# the mixed data set and on each density regime separately, with the test
# RMSEs of SI Tables S1-S3. The body-order decompositions and DMRG
# benchmarks are analyses of the reference and the models, not metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-chong2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Chong et al. (2026): resolving the body-order paradox of machine-learning interatomic potentials" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-chong2026 .

entity:article-chong2026 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:sameAs <https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0303302> ;
    schema:datePublished "2026"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:name "Resolving the body-order paradox of machine learning interatomic potentials" ;
